s, input validation, JSON encoding into testable functions with clear error handling. Keep external behavior identical: same status codes, same response bodies. Need full refactored file. Need likely define sentinel errors: errInvalidID, errUserNotFound, errDatabase? But external behavior: 400 body {\"error\":\"bad id\"} no Content-Type? Original 400/404/500 do not set Content-Type. Success sets Content-Type application/json and encodes map. JSON encoder adds newline. Need preserve exact bodies? For success, json.Encoder.Encode(map[string]string{\"name\": name, \"email\": email}) produces {\"email\":\"...\",\"name\":\"...\"}\\n? Go map keys sorted alphabetically: email then name. Need preserve. If we use json.Marshal(map[string]string{...}) and write, no newline. That changes body. Need keep same response bodies. Could use json.NewEncoder(w).Encode(user) for success. But if user struct with fields Name, Email", "top2": [[[1596, -0.0030493689700961113], [760, -6.889895915985107]], [[1144, -1.2755474926962052e-05], [14235, -12.074366569519043]], [[4087, -0.013568666763603687], [310, -4.484502792358398]], [[1156, -0.04033331573009491], [303, -3.381929874420166]], [[579, -0.21128802001476288], [25, -2.38045072555542]], [[1622, -0.0032567307353019714], [3296, -6.493985176086426]], [[13, -0.34628215432167053], [25, -1.6424285173416138]], [[14235, -0.03151596710085869], [1165, -4.241366386413574]], [[89109, -0.329047828912735], [7936, -1.8127838373184204]], [[5805, -0.00022598674695473164], [2400, -8.819626808166504]], [[9830, -0.023745335638523102], [6795, -3.803875684738159]], [[6795, -2.8133788873674348e-05], [17369, -11.95277214050293]], [[1083, -1.4613499641418457], [47781, -1.5564216375350952]], [[1228, -0.09712269902229309], [2400, -2.7817158699035645]], [[470, -3.171017306158319e-05], [5568, -10.634215354919434]], [[5568, -0.0028812033124268055], [74243, -6.180710792541504]], [[440, -0.9110299944877625], [25, -1.8859273195266724]], [[2708, -0.036327388137578964], [